  "tier": "told-once",
  "plain": "Nuno Loureiro, a fusion scientist Michels calls \"the tip of the spear\" on magnetic reconnection, a key problem in making nuclear fusion work, was shot at his home on December 15, 2025, went into surgery that evening and was pronounced dead the next morning. Michels tells it himself, naming Claudio Neves Valente as the shooter and citing a Department of Justice transcript of Valente's videos; he places the home in Brookline, Massachusetts, though at one point says Brooklyn, New York. Arguing with a skeptic, he rejects the idea that the killing, or the case of Carl Grillmair, is \"a non-story,\" seeing it as part of a pattern of top scientists going missing or dying."
}
